The amendment defines an “Export Agricultural Crop” as any crop that:

- has export potential **in addition to local consumption**;  
- is **not** one of the excluded categories – paddy, vegetables, fruits, root crops, other food crops, or a plantation crop;  
- is **declared by the Minister** in charge of the subject as a “notified agricultural crop” under section 2 of the Act.  

[045/2026 §5]
